# clusters/@@CLUSTER@@/agents/netpol-cluster-admin-egress.yaml
#
# Rendered by the propose-cluster-admin skill (F4 cascade). The per-tier DEFAULT-DENY egress
# NetworkPolicy for @@CLUSTER@@'s cluster-admin agent pod (03 §10). It selects every cluster-admin pod
# by the tier label the controller stamps on the pod template (`kube-agents/tier: cluster-admin`), so
# it needs no agent-name knowledge. Applied in the `agents/` wave alongside the identity + CR.
#
# SHAPE = PURE ALLOWLIST. policyTypes:[Egress] with a podSelector makes egress default-deny; only the
# CIDRs/ports below are reachable. The cloud metadata server (169.254.169.254) and arbitrary hosts are
# UNREACHABLE with no explicit block rule (the 03 §11 egress negative). There is deliberately NO
# 0.0.0.0/0 rule.
#
# CROSS-CLUSTER CONTRACT (05 §5): a spoke consumes exactly two hub services — Inference (LiteLLM,
# per-tier virtual key) and Minty (the GitHub/Workload-Identity token broker) — over VPC-internal
# private endpoints, plus cloud APIs, GitHub, and the MCP grounding endpoints. No cross-cluster
# Kubernetes credentials ever.
#
# LIMITATION (hostname precision): NetworkPolicy is L3/L4 — GitHub/MCP are allowlisted by IP CIDR (which
# drifts). The hostname-precise L7 egress proxy is a Phase 5 hardening item (07).
#
# GKE Workload Identity note (flagged for production): on GKE, WI tokens are fetched via the GKE metadata
# server (169.254.169.254), which this policy does NOT allow — WI's metadata concealment already blocks
# the node-SA paths, and the load-bearing negative is that the RAW cloud metadata is unreachable. If your
# agent acquires GCP tokens via the metadata server rather than Minty, add a NARROW allow to
# 169.254.169.254/32:988 (WI only) or adopt the Phase 5 L7 proxy. On Kind there is no metadata server.
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: cluster-admin-egress
  namespace: kubeagents-system
  labels:
    kube-agents/tier: cluster-admin
    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: gitops
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      kube-agents/tier: cluster-admin
  policyTypes:
    - Egress
  egress:
    # 1) DNS — cluster resolution. Without this, every name-based egress fails before it starts.
    - to:
        - namespaceSelector:
            matchLabels:
              kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system
      ports:
        - protocol: UDP
          port: 53
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 53
    # 2) Hub Inference (LiteLLM) — the ONLY inference path (per-tier virtual key), VPC-internal private.
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: @@HUB_INFERENCE_CIDR@@
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 443
    # 3) Hub Minty — the Workload-Identity / GitHub token broker, VPC-internal private. Short-lived,
    #    scoped tokens only; the agent holds no long-lived write credentials.
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: @@HUB_MINTY_CIDR@@
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 443
    # 4) Google cloud APIs via Private Google Access (restricted.googleapis.com). Reads only. This ALSO
    #    carries the eventingress Pub/Sub SUBSCRIBE leg (Phase 4 D1, 04 §4): pubsub.googleapis.com
    #    resolves to the same restricted VIP, so draining PRE-CREATED alert/GitHub subscriptions needs
    #    no new CIDR/port. Subscribe-only — eventingress never creates a topic/subscription and never
    #    publishes; the invariant (read-only, GitOps-only writes) is unchanged.
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: 199.36.153.8/30
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 443
    # 5) GitHub — push suggestion branches / open PRs (submit-suggestion) with a Minty-minted token.
    #    Allowlisted by GitHub's published IP ranges (https://api.github.com/meta).
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: @@GITHUB_CIDRS@@
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 443
    # 6) MCP grounding endpoints the agent reads live docs from (developer_knowledge, gke — 03 §10).
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: @@MCP_GROUNDING_CIDRS@@
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 443
